WEBVTT

NOTE
Tutorial: utilities-metering
Generated: 2026-09-28T04:37:30.576Z
Source of truth: docs/tutorials/utilities-metering.md — edit there and re-record.

1
00:00:02.301 --> 00:00:06.806
At month end every water and electricity
meter gets read. Here's this month —

2
00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:08.306
nothing read yet.

3
00:00:09.088 --> 00:00:13.144
Group by unit to follow the caretaker's
walk: each door's water and power

4
00:00:13.144 --> 00:00:15.088
together, the KPLC bulk meter last.

5
00:00:17.298 --> 00:00:21.880
At a desk it's a table: type the reading,
press Enter, and you're on the next meter.

6
00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:23.380
Usage appears as you type.

7
00:00:29.686 --> 00:00:33.851
Save them in one go. On a phone, the
caretaker gets cards with a camera button

8
00:00:33.851 --> 00:00:35.351
for a photo of each dial.

9
00:00:36.334 --> 00:00:40.713
Readings on paper? Download sheet gives
this month's meters in walking order, with

10
00:00:40.713 --> 00:00:42.213
last month's numbers.

11
00:00:46.063 --> 00:00:50.922
Fill in the Current reading column and
import it. Every row is matched to its

12
00:00:50.922 --> 00:00:52.563
meter and previewed first.

13
00:00:53.715 --> 00:00:58.215
Imported readings arrive as Submitted,
waiting for a manager's approval.

14
00:01:05.843 --> 00:01:10.906
On Review & bill the manager checks last
month's readings, and any photos, before

15
00:01:10.906 --> 00:01:12.406
approving them.

16
00:01:12.988 --> 00:01:16.988
Unusual jumps are flagged — worth a second
look before you approve.

17
00:01:22.244 --> 00:01:26.244
Approving fixes the rate and the charge
for each reading.

18
00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:34.294
Then bill: readings go onto next month's
rent invoice — or a separate utilities

19
00:01:34.294 --> 00:01:36.290
invoice if that one's already paid.

20
00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:44.644
Paid & unpaid is the chase list: per
tenant, water and electricity billed, paid

21
00:01:44.644 --> 00:01:46.144
and still owing.

22
00:01:46.685 --> 00:01:51.185
Tick who owes and email reminders — or
export to Excel or PDF.

23
00:01:56.997 --> 00:02:01.452
Reconciliation shows where the money goes.
Water: what tenants paid against the

24
00:02:01.452 --> 00:02:04.497
council bill — the borehole surplus goes
to the owner.

25
00:02:05.646 --> 00:02:11.141
Power: the KPLC bulk meter against units
billed, vacant units and common areas, so

26
00:02:11.141 --> 00:02:12.641
losses show up.

27
00:02:12.641 --> 00:02:16.770
Tenants see their readings and what they
owe in their portal, so nobody has to call

28
00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:18.270
to ask.

29
00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:20.674
That's metering: read, approve, bill,
chase.
